1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:00,728
Hello!

2
00:00:00,728 --> 00:00:03,655
This week you will practise three things:

3
00:00:03,655 --> 00:00:07,510
matching headings to paragraphs, completing summaries,

4
00:00:07,510 --> 00:00:11,436
and learning vocabulary for the environment and health.

5
00:00:12,736 --> 00:00:13,462
Point one:

6
00:00:13,462 --> 00:00:14,769
Matching Headings.

7
00:00:14,769 --> 00:00:20,214
A heading sums up the main idea of the whole paragraph, not a small detail.

8
00:00:20,214 --> 00:00:25,223
Read the first sentence and the last sentence, and then ask yourself:

9
00:00:25,223 --> 00:00:27,328
what is this paragraph doing?

10
00:00:28,628 --> 00:00:31,340
What is the whole paragraph doing?

11
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:39,502
The most common trap is choosing a heading just because it shares a word with the

12
00:00:39,502 --> 00:00:40,164
paragraph.

13
00:00:40,164 --> 00:00:43,142
For example, a paragraph mentions boats once,

14
00:00:43,142 --> 00:00:46,452
but it is really about people changing their jobs.

15
00:00:47,752 --> 00:00:53,032
The town once relied on fishing, but now most people work in a factory.

16
00:00:56,332 --> 00:00:57,082
Point two:

17
00:00:57,082 --> 00:00:58,507
Summary Completion.

18
00:00:58,507 --> 00:01:04,732
Before you look for the answer, predict whether the missing word is a noun, a verb,

19
00:01:04,732 --> 00:01:05,932
or an adjective.

20
00:01:05,932 --> 00:01:10,132
Then check the word limit and copy the spelling exactly.

21
00:01:11,432 --> 00:01:14,720
After the word to, we need a base verb.

22
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:18,496
Point three:

23
00:01:18,496 --> 00:01:22,643
Yes, No, Not Given asks about the writer's opinion.

24
00:01:22,643 --> 00:01:25,895
True, False, Not Given asks about facts.

25
00:01:25,895 --> 00:01:32,400
If the writer only reports events and gives no opinion, the answer is Not Given.

26
00:01:33,700 --> 00:01:36,988
I would argue that the plan is too risky.

27
00:01:40,288 --> 00:01:41,483
Point four:

28
00:01:41,483 --> 00:01:42,678
vocabulary.

29
00:01:42,678 --> 00:01:45,829
First, the environment group.

30
00:01:45,829 --> 00:01:48,328
Please repeat after me.

31
00:01:49,628 --> 00:01:51,421
Biodiversity.

32
00:01:51,421 --> 00:01:52,524
Habitat.

33
00:01:52,524 --> 00:01:54,455
Cut emissions.

34
00:01:54,455 --> 00:01:57,764
Sustainable development.

35
00:02:01,064 --> 00:02:03,584
A sedentary lifestyle.

36
00:02:03,584 --> 00:02:05,417
Chronic illness.

37
00:02:05,417 --> 00:02:07,594
Disease prevention.

38
00:02:07,594 --> 00:02:09,656
Mental well-being.

39
00:02:12,956 --> 00:02:16,307
Four common mistakes for Vietnamese learners.

40
00:02:16,307 --> 00:02:16,605
One:

41
00:02:16,605 --> 00:02:19,956
choosing a heading because it repeats a word.

42
00:02:19,956 --> 00:02:20,254
Two:

43
00:02:20,254 --> 00:02:24,126
writing two words when the question allows only one.

44
00:02:24,126 --> 00:02:24,573
Three:

45
00:02:24,573 --> 00:02:28,519
changing the word form when copying from the passage.

46
00:02:28,519 --> 00:02:28,892
Four:

47
00:02:28,892 --> 00:02:34,700
answering No when the writer only reports events, when it should be Not Given.

48
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:37,237
Quiz one:

49
00:02:37,237 --> 00:02:42,149
the instruction says ONE WORD ONLY, and you write the river.

50
00:02:42,149 --> 00:02:44,195
Is that correct or wrong?

51
00:02:44,195 --> 00:02:44,932
Quiz two:

52
00:02:44,932 --> 00:02:51,072
the writer only reports that the council banned cars, and gives no opinion.

53
00:02:51,072 --> 00:02:52,464
The statement is:

54
00:02:52,464 --> 00:02:55,411
the writer believes the ban is wise.

55
00:02:55,411 --> 00:02:57,212
Yes, No, or Not Given?

56
00:03:01,512 --> 00:03:02,451
Quiz three:

57
00:03:02,451 --> 00:03:06,120
what do we call a long period with no rain?

58
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:07,827
Drought, or erosion?

59
00:03:07,827 --> 00:03:10,728
Choose before you hear the answer.

60
00:03:14,028 --> 00:03:14,742
Answers.

61
00:03:14,742 --> 00:03:15,099
One:

62
00:03:15,099 --> 00:03:18,490
wrong, because the river is two words.

63
00:03:18,490 --> 00:03:18,847
Two:

64
00:03:18,847 --> 00:03:24,024
Not Given, because the writer does not express an opinion.

65
00:03:24,024 --> 00:03:24,559
Three:

66
00:03:24,559 --> 00:03:28,040
drought, which means a long dry period.

67
00:03:28,040 --> 00:03:31,788
Erosion is when soil or rock is worn away.

68
00:03:34,088 --> 00:03:34,617
Summary:

69
00:03:34,617 --> 00:03:37,925
a heading is the main idea of the whole paragraph,

70
00:03:37,925 --> 00:03:42,159
a summary needs a predicted word class and the right word limit,

71
00:03:42,159 --> 00:03:46,526
and for opinion questions you look for signals such as in my view.

72
00:03:46,526 --> 00:03:51,950
Do the week six exercises in the app, time yourself at twenty minutes per passage,

73
00:03:51,950 --> 00:03:56,912
and review vocabulary on a schedule of day one, three, seven, and fourteen.
